					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13644453#post-4760370</guid>
				<title>Re: The wrong angle.</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13644453/scp-063-j#post-4760370</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2020 22:35:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Riemann</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1787775</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>You know, to be perfectly honest, I thought the same thing starting out. But after 5 revisions, it was either too preachy (it's hard to convey that sort of information and keep it interesting in this context!), too oblique, or not funny.</p> <p>So I switched tacks, and now this balances between quite a lot of nebulous punchlines, one of which happens to be that spherical geometries are common.</p> <p>If you're ever on IRC, hop on to #site17 and give me a ping, I'd be happy to talk out any ideas on improving this joke but keeping it appropriate for a wide audience :)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
