				<wikidot:authorName>Suspicious Mr Guy</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3481354</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>(Badum tss)<br /> It's a good <em>idea</em>, but the execution is way off for me. It feels way too on the nose, and I've seen a lot of scps that are just &quot;normal object but stupid people call it an scp&quot;. I'm sure there's a great way to make a -J that's suposed to be non-euclid, but this doesn't feel like it.</p> <p>-1</p> 
				 	]]>
